    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The Right to Repair movement is a direct assault on corporate monopolies that profit from keeping consumers in a perpetual state of dependency on expensive, proprietary parts. By forcing manufacturers to lock out independent technicians and third-party parts, these companies artificially inflate repair costs and extend the lifespan of electronic waste, which is a massive environmental and economic burden on the average person. This fight is essential because it restores consumer sovereignty, allowing individuals to choose who fixes their devices rather than being forced to buy new ones at the whim of a greedy corporation. Ultimately, supporting Right to Repair is about breaking the cycle of planned obsolescence and ensuring that technology serves people instead of the other way around.",
